# Secrets and local machine state
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.key
**/*.pem
.DS_Store
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Client/private artifacts never belong in the workflow repository.
**/personas/
**/input/
**/output/
**/clients/

# Rawy private operator state. The shell is tracked; customer data is not.
/Rawy/Clients/
/Rawy/.rawy/
# Generated from client notes, so it carries real client names and book titles.
/Rawy/Archive.md

# The Codex image skill is installed per user; never commit an absolute symlink.
.cursor/skills/codex-imagegen

# Obsidian: the vault config is shared, the per-machine pane state is not.
# A pattern with a slash is anchored, so Rawy needs its own entries.
**/.obsidian/workspace.json
**/.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/graph-state.json
.trash/

# Scratch renders and proofs. These are pages of real books.
tmp/

# Local tool caches, regenerated on demand.
.impeccable/

# One-off client build scripts. They carry a home-directory project path, real
# persona photo filenames, and a whole client prompt pack — none of which may
# enter a tracked file (AGENTS.md, "Data boundaries"). Sanitize into a general
# builder before tracking anything like this.
tools/scripts/build_abdullah_prompts.py
tools/scripts/build_abdullah2_prompts.py

# Copyrighted source material and derived local research stay local.
tools/.corpus/
